  "goodToKnow": "Melancholisch means melancholy or wistful: eine melancholische Stimmung, ein melancholischer Blick. Die Melancholie is melancholy, once explained by black bile (Greek melaina chole) in the theory of four temperaments; der Melancholiker is a melancholic person. Albrecht Dürer's engraving Melencolia I (1514) is a famous image of it. Synonyms: schwermütig, wehmütig, trübsinnig."
